{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.404, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10936, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1036, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01NXYsoRahJxKYTE2wEtuV2o", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray analysis sets a one-sided 95% upper limit where 2[ln L_max − ln L(<σv>_95)] = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, or 1.355 in log-likelihood). The AMS-02 antiproton analysis instead uses the upper endpoint of the ΔQ = 3.84 region (Q = −2lnL). The paper calls 3.84 the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold and notes it differs from the common one-sided 2.71 prescription. Nuisance parameters: the dSph analysis profiles over each dwarf's J-factor, using a Gaussian prior on log10 s with J = s·J0 and s ranging over log10 s ∈ [−3,3]. The antiproton analysis profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, using a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197 and a profiling range of 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T075413Z_dev-02_staged_20c3", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray analysis sets a one-sided 95% upper limit where 2[ln L_max − ln L(<σv>_95)] = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, or 1.355 in log-likelihood). The AMS-02 antiproton analysis instead uses the upper endpoint of the ΔQ = 3.84 region (Q = −2lnL). The paper calls 3.84 the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold and notes it differs from the common one-sided 2.71 prescription. Nuisance parameters: the dSph analysis profiles over each dwarf's J-factor, using a Gaussian prior on log10 s with J = s·J0 and s ranging over log10 s ∈ [−3,3]. The antiproton analysis profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, using a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197 and a profiling range of 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 11.523, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1356, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25367, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T07:54:24+00:00"}
